speechtext:
The house in committee of ways and means, Sir Eugene Fiset in the chair.
Customs tariff-443, Apparatus designed for cooking or for heating buildings.
(1)	For coal or wood: British preferential tariff, free: intermediate tariff, 22| per cent; general tariff, 25 per cent;
(2)	For gas: British preferential tariff, free: intermediate tariff, 221 per cent; general tariff, 30 per cent;
(3)	For electricity: British preferential tariff, free; intermediate tariff, 224 per cent; general tariff, 25 per cent;
(4)	For oil: British preferential tariff, free; intermediate tariff, 221 per cent; general tariff, 25 per cent;
(5)	N.o.p.: British preferential tariff, free; intermediate tariff, 221 per cent; general tariff, 25 per cent.
